2 CONT
2 CONT Another of the old-timers of the Wetaskiwin district passed away on Saturday last in the person of Ole Kjorlin. He had been quite poorly for some time, and was aged fifty-five years and ten months. Deceased came to this district a
2 CONC bout twenty-five years ago and took up a homestead near Falun, where he resided until about three years ago, when he moved to the Crooked Lake district. He was always of a jovial disposition and had a very large circle of friends 
2 CONC and acquaintances. He leaves a widow and large grown-up family. The funeral was held at the Wang church on Monday, the service being conducted by Rev. Lee. It was one of the largest funerals ever held in the community, and the flo
2 CONC ral tributes were especially numerous and beautiful. The interment was in the Wang cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Wetaskiwin Times, November 1, 1923
