1 NOTE He attended the University of Chicago before volunteering to serve in the Air Force during WWII. He 
2 CONT rose to the rank of Major and was a bomb formation leader flying missions in Europe and the Pacific. 
2 CONT His main Aircraft was the B-26. After the war, he attended Columbia University where he was 
2 CONT approached and convinced to volunteer to train pilots for the Jews in Palestine. After the formation of 
2 CONT the state of Israel, he chose to remain there and met his wife Eve Davidowitz and they were married in 
2 CONT 1949. Trygve later served as a test pilot for the Israeli airlines Arkia and El-Al. He was an amateur 
2 CONT archeologist and poet.
