2 CONT Nøtterøy Gårds og Slekthistorie (Unneberg 1971) s.925 (Grindrønningen), 962 (Tangli)
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://newspaperarchive.com/sterling-standard/1891-11-19/page-3 Sterling standard, Thursday 19.November 1891, page 3]:
2 CONT
2 CONT A fatal accident occurred on the C&NW (Chicago & North Western Railway) Saturday morning three miles east of Fulton Junction. As the Sterling passenger was speeding along at the rate of 20 miles an hour and while passing a gang of
2 CONC  bridge laborers, one of them, a man named Waldheim(?) stepped in front of the engine, was struck by the pilot and instantly killed. The deceased was a Norwegian, had been in this country but 18 months, was aged 41 years and leave
2 CONC s a wife and five children in his native country, to which he expected to return next month. No blame was attached to the railway employee. The man appeared to be dazed, and deliberatly stepped from the north to the south track, a
2 CONC nd to his death. The coroners jury rendered a verdict in accordance with the above facts.
2 CONT
